"feedback": {"neutral": "<p>The traceback is a report, and it is meant to be read: it names where the program stopped (line 3 of party.py), the statement it stopped in, and why&mdash;a division by zero, so groups was zero. The file name says where that line is, not that the file is missing; Python read the line perfectly well and stopped because the division could not be done, so nothing was skipped; and the traceback is printed by Python when it gives up, not by the program.</p>"}
