The course name and the item titles are the join keys between the
tangled files: if a title changes in a quiz, this dictionary is the
only other place to change---and they live in the same source, side by
side.
Canvas prefixes the report's columns with item identifiers, so we match
columns by containment rather than equality---which is also why no
item title may be contained in another.

The school answers are open text as well, and they go on the coding
sheet with the rest, since the sheet is where the coder has them to
look up; but they are not among the answers the model pre-codes, as
which huvudman ran a school is settled by the register rather than by a
judgement anything could suggest.
Hence two lists where one would do: the prompt below is built from
[[CODED_OPEN_ITEMS]], the sheet from [[OPEN_ITEMS]].

