@

A roster we cannot read is a reason to fall back, not to stop: the
analysis of the answers themselves does not need the identity, and a
missing enrolment scope or an expired token should not cost us the
summaries.
So the failure is announced and the rows are left as they came.

<<index the roster by every identifier it offers>>=
by_id, by_sis, by_name = {}, {}, {}
try:
    students = list(course.get_users(enrollment_type=["student"]))
except Exception as error:
    print(f"warning: cannot read the roster of {COURSE}: {error}")
    return
for user in students:
    login = getattr(user, "login_id", None)
    if not login:
        continue
    by_id[str(user.id)] = login
    sis = getattr(user, "sis_user_id", None)
    if sis:
        by_sis[str(sis)] = login
    by_name.setdefault(user.name, []).append(login)
@

A roster entry without a login ID is skipped rather than indexed under
its name: indexing it would make a name that belongs to one usable
student look ambiguous, and we would refuse a lookup we could have
made.

The report's column headings are Canvas's, so we find the two ID
columns by name once and reuse them for every row.
The three lookups are tried in turn and the first that answers wins,
which is also the order of how much we trust them.
A row that none of them answers is left without the column, which is
exactly what [[student_of]] reads as \enquote{fall back}.

<<look each row up in that index>>=
if not rows:
    return
id_column = next((c for c in rows[0] if c.strip().lower() == "id"), None)
sis_column = next((c for c in rows[0]
                   if c.strip().lower() == "sis_id"), None)
for row in rows:
    login = None
    if id_column and row.get(id_column):
        login = by_id.get(str(row[id_column]).strip())
    if not login and sis_column and row.get(sis_column):
        login = by_sis.get(str(row[sis_column]).strip())
    if not login:
        candidates = by_name.get(row[STUDENT], [])
        if len(candidates) == 1:
            login = candidates[0]
        elif len(candidates) > 1:
            print(f"warning: several students in {COURSE} are named"
                  f" {row[STUDENT]!r} and the report has no usable ID"
                  f" column; falling back to the name, which cannot"
                  f" tell them apart")
    if login:
        row[LOGIN_COLUMN] = login
