The test file gets an entry point of its own, so that
[[python3 test_analyze_quiz.py]] is a complete check without any
framework installed.
It collects by the [[test_]] prefix rather than by a list of names, so
that a test added above needs no second edit here to be run---the
failure mode of a hand-kept list is a test that quietly stops being
run, which is the same class of silent failure the login IDs are here
to prevent.

<<run the tests without a framework>>=
def main():
    """Run every test function in this module."""
    tests = sorted(
        (name, function)
        for name, function in globals().items()
        if name.startswith("test_") and callable(function)
    )
    for name, function in tests:
        function()
        print(f"ok {name}")
    print(f"{len(tests)} tests passed")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
